  "id": "eye-movement-desensitization-and-reprocessing",
  "term": "eye-movement desensitization and reprocessing",
  "definition": "Eye movement desensitization and reprocessing (EMDR) is a psychotherapy used for post-traumatic stress disorder that is described as evidence-based and effective. It is a relatively recent therapy, and debate has focused in part on whether its bilateral stimulation is an active ingredient in how it works.",
